# Privacy Policy — Yaser USMLE

**Effective date:** October 20, 2026  
**App:** Yaser USMLE (mobile)  
**Website:** [https://yaser-usmle.com](https://yaser-usmle.com)  

This policy explains how the Yaser USMLE mobile app handles personal information. It applies to the Android and iOS apps. The website may have its own notices; this document describes the mobile app.

Yaser USMLE is a student app for USMLE preparation: accounts, courses, lessons, exams, flashcards, study plans, payments, and notifications.

---

## 1. Information we collect

### Account information

When you register, sign in, or update your profile, we process:

- Full name
- Email address
- Password (sent to our server to create or verify your account; the app does not keep your password in plain text)
- Phone number, if you provide one
- Profile photo URL, if your account has one

### Learning activity

While you use the app, our servers store data needed to run the service, including:

- Courses, lessons, and packages you open or enroll in
- Exam answers, scores, and results
- Flashcard reviews and study-plan progress
- In-app notifications
- Trial-session data if you use a trial without a full account

### Payments

Checkout is reviewed by our team. Depending on the method you choose, we collect:

- Country and payment method
- Amount, currency, and coupon code
- Name, phone, and account email included with the payment note
- A photo of your payment receipt or Stripe invoice, chosen from your photo library
- The email you used for a Stripe card payment, if that method applies

We do not collect or store your full card number in the app. Card payments are completed on Stripe’s own page. You then upload proof so we can match the payment to your account.

### Device and session data

- A device identifier created on your phone (`device fingerprint`) and a device name, sent when you register or sign in, so we can manage sessions
- Access and refresh tokens stored in the device’s secure storage
- A cached copy of your profile on the device so the app can open while you are signed in
- Language preference (Arabic or English)
- Network connection status, used only to show when you are offline
- Push notification token (Firebase Cloud Messaging) and platform (`android` or `ios`), sent to our server after you sign in so we can deliver course and account alerts
- Files you download for offline video or lesson materials, stored on your device

### Information we do not collect

The app does not request your location, contacts, microphone, or camera. It does not include advertising SDKs or a third-party analytics SDK. We do not sell personal information.

---

## 2. How we use information

We use the information above to:

- Create and secure your account, including password reset
- Show your courses, lessons, exams, flashcards, and study progress
- Process enrollments and review payment proof
- Send push notifications you allow, and in-app notifications
- Remember your language and keep you signed in
- Detect and limit unauthorized use of an account
- Respond when you contact us from the in-app Contact screen, WhatsApp, or email

---

## 3. Permissions

| Permission | Why |
| --- | --- |
| Internet and network state | Load courses, sign in, and detect offline mode |
| Notifications | Course and account alerts, if you allow them |
| Photos / storage (images) | Let you pick a payment-receipt image from your gallery |
| Foreground service | Keep video downloads running on Android |

You can deny notifications or photo access. Sign-in and browsing still work; alerts or receipt upload will not.

---

## 4. Sharing with service providers

We share data only as needed to operate the app:

| Provider | Role |
| --- | --- |
| Yaser USMLE servers (`api.yaser-usmle.com`) | Accounts, courses, exams, payments, and notifications |
| Google Firebase Cloud Messaging | Delivers push notifications to your device |
| VdoCipher | Secure course video playback and offline video |
| YouTube | Plays or downloads lesson videos that are hosted on YouTube |
| Stripe | Processes card payments on Stripe’s site when you choose that method |
| Google Fonts | Loads typefaces used in the interface |

WhatsApp, Telegram, and social links in the app open those services only if you tap them. We do not send your account data to those apps automatically.

We may also disclose information if the law requires it, or to protect students, staff, or the service from fraud or abuse.

---

## 5. Storage and security

- Sign-in tokens are kept in encrypted device storage (`flutter_secure_storage`).
- Profile cache, language, and similar preferences use local app storage.
- Offline videos and files stay on your device until you remove them.
- Traffic to our API uses HTTPS.
- Payment receipt images are uploaded to our server so an admin can confirm the payment.

No method of transmission or storage is perfectly secure. Use a strong password and sign out on shared devices.

---

## 6. How long we keep data

- Account, enrollment, exam, and payment records are kept while your account is active and as long as we need them for teaching records, payment disputes, and legal obligations.
- The push token is removed from our server when you sign out (best effort) and when Firebase rotates it.
- Local tokens, cached profile, and downloaded files are deleted from the device when you sign out or uninstall the app, except downloads you remove separately and anything the operating system keeps in backups.

---

## 7. Your choices

- Update your name and phone in account settings.
- Change your password in the app, or use “Forgot password.”
- Turn off notifications in the system settings for Yaser USMLE.
- Decline photo access if you do not want to upload a receipt from the gallery.
- Sign out to clear session tokens on that device.
- Ask us to access, correct, or delete your account using the contact methods below. We may need to keep payment records where the law requires it.

---

## 8. Children

Yaser USMLE is for students preparing for the USMLE. It is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has created an account, contact us and we will delete it.

---

## 9. International transfers

Our servers and the providers listed above may process data outside your country, including the United States (Google, YouTube, Stripe) and the regions where our API is hosted. We use this data to provide the app you requested.

---

## 10. Changes

We will update the “Effective date” at the top when this policy changes. Continued use of the app after an update means you accept the revised policy. For a material change, we may also show a notice in the app.

---

## 11. Contact

Questions about this policy or your data:

- In the app: **Profile → Contact us**
- Website: [https://yaser-usmle.com](https://yaser-usmle.com)

The contact email and phone shown in the app come from our public site settings and are the current way to reach us.

